WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.348
Mary Jane was so sweet that I didn't want to tell her I had put the money in her uncle's coffin.

2
00:00:08.349 --> 00:00:12.318
So I said to her, "I'll write it on a piece of paper.

3
00:00:12.319 --> 00:00:17.032
After I leave town, you can read it. Then you'll know where to look."

4
00:00:17.033 --> 00:00:20.358
Mary Jane gave me some paper and I scribbled:

5
00:00:20.359 --> 00:00:28.172
"I was behind the door and I saw you crying. I felt very sorry for you. I put it in the coffin."

6
00:00:28.173 --> 00:00:31.480
Then I folded up the paper and gave it to her.

7
00:00:31.481 --> 00:00:36.429
I didn't think it would be safe for me and Jim to travel on the river in daylight.

8
00:00:36.430 --> 00:00:39.599
I wanted to wait until dark to get away.

9
00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:46.072
But Mary Jane was such an honest person that I knew she would not be able to hide her feelings all day.

10
00:00:46.073 --> 00:00:51.528
The expression on her face would tell the king and the duke that she knew the truth.

11
00:00:51.529 --> 00:00:55.525
I asked Mary Jane if she could leave the house until evening.

12
00:00:55.526 --> 00:00:59.248
She agreed to visit her friend Hannah Proctor.

13
00:00:59.249 --> 00:01:02.810
She left quickly before the king and the duke woke up.

14
00:01:02.811 --> 00:01:11.321
At breakfast, I told everyone that Hannah Proctor had the mumps and explained that Mary Jane had gone to look after her.

15
00:01:11.322 --> 00:01:15.516
In the afternoon, I watched the auction in the town square.

16
00:01:15.517 --> 00:01:21.120
By late in the day, almost everything belonging to Peter Wilks had been sold.

17
00:01:21.121 --> 00:01:25.246
But I knew that no money would be paid on the day of the auction.

18
00:01:25.247 --> 00:01:29.538
The duke and the king would have to stay for another day to collect it.

19
00:01:29.539 --> 00:01:33.702
Before that could happen, Mary Jane would come back.

20
00:01:33.703 --> 00:01:38.163
She would tell the truth, and the two scoundrels would be arrested.

21
00:01:38.164 --> 00:01:42.157
By then, I would be safe on the river again with Jim.

22
00:01:42.158 --> 00:01:47.215
I was quite proud of myself and thought I had arranged things very well.

23
00:01:47.216 --> 00:01:51.748
Then I heard loud voices coming toward the center of town.

24
00:01:51.749 --> 00:01:59.011
I turned and saw a well-dressed older gentleman and a nice-looking younger one with his right arm in a sling.

25
00:01:59.012 --> 00:02:08.442
Some townspeople were with them, and one of them called out, "Here are two more men who say they are Harvey Wilks and his brother William!"

26
00:02:08.443 --> 00:02:14.555
Wouldn't you think that the king and the duke would give up when they saw the real Englishmen?

27
00:02:14.556 --> 00:02:25.363
Well, they didn't! The king said in an angry voice, "These men are liars trying to steal our property. Don't listen to them!"

28
00:02:25.364 --> 00:02:33.788
I could see that some townspeople believed the king, but Doctor Robinson and some others looked pleased to see the newcomers.

29
00:02:33.789 --> 00:02:38.248
They had never believed that the duke and the king were honest men.

30
00:02:38.249 --> 00:02:42.560
The two new arrivals were very confused by the uproar.

31
00:02:42.561 --> 00:02:45.880
Harvey Wilks, the older gentleman, told their story:

32
00:02:45.881 --> 00:02:53.897
They had come all the way from England to see their dying brother, but they had been delayed when poor William broke his arm.

33
00:02:53.898 --> 00:02:57.663
The king demanded to see written proof of who they were.

34
00:02:57.664 --> 00:03:03.366
Harvey replied that this was impossible because their bags had been lost on the journey.

35
00:03:03.367 --> 00:03:08.966
So it went on for a while with both pairs of men claiming they were the true relatives.

36
00:03:08.967 --> 00:03:13.812
I knew the truth, but if I told it, I'd be in trouble too.

37
00:03:13.813 --> 00:03:17.569
Then I wouldn’t be able to get away and help Jim.

38
00:03:17.570 --> 00:03:24.081
Finally, Harvey Wilks said that Peter, his brother, had a small tattoo on his chest.

39
00:03:24.082 --> 00:03:33.418
He challenged the king to describe it. "Why, yes," said the king, "he has a small lightning bolt on his chest."

40
00:03:33.419 --> 00:03:39.902
"No," said the old gentleman. "It is his initials: P and W."

41
00:03:39.903 --> 00:03:46.374
By now, most of the townspeople were so confused that they did not know what to believe.

42
00:03:46.375 --> 00:03:51.072
Doctor Robinson jumped up onto the table that had been used for the auction.

43
00:03:51.073 --> 00:03:54.672
"There's only one way to settle this," he shouted.

44
00:03:54.673 --> 00:03:58.241
"Let's all go to the cemetery and dig up the corpse.

45
00:03:58.242 --> 00:04:02.310
Grab the four men and the boy and make them come with us."

46
00:04:02.311 --> 00:04:08.112
I was very scared, but a townsman was holding me so hard that I couldn't escape.

47
00:04:08.113 --> 00:04:16.183
"If we don't find the tattoo those two scoundrels described, we'll hang you along with them!" he growled at me.

48
00:04:16.184 --> 00:04:21.395
It was dark and windy in the cemetery, and lightning flashed in the sky.

49
00:04:21.396 --> 00:04:26.291
So many men were helping that it did not take long to dig up the grave.

50
00:04:26.292 --> 00:04:29.619
Then they pulled out the coffin and opened the lid.

51
00:04:29.620 --> 00:04:38.066
A huge lightning bolt lit up the night, and someone yelled, "Look at that—there's a big bag of gold on his chest!"

52
00:04:38.067 --> 00:04:42.726
Everyone became so excited that they rushed toward the coffin.

53
00:04:42.727 --> 00:04:49.454
The townsman forgot to hold my wrist, and I ran away at once, down the road as fast as I could.

54
00:04:49.455 --> 00:04:52.813
I ran right through town without seeing anyone.

55
00:04:52.814 --> 00:04:59.249
When I got to the riverbank, a lightning flash showed me a canoe that was pulled up on shore.

56
00:04:59.250 --> 00:05:03.950
I jumped in and paddled until I came to the raft where Jim was waiting.

57
00:05:03.951 --> 00:05:08.031
I had never been so glad to see anyone in my whole life.

58
00:05:08.032 --> 00:05:12.979
"Cut the rope loose and let's go, Jim!" I yelled, climbing aboard.

59
00:05:12.980 --> 00:05:17.385
"We're finally free of those scoundrels."

60
00:05:17.386 --> 00:05:20.655
In seconds, we were out on the river again.

61
00:05:20.656 --> 00:05:25.276
I felt so relieved that I began to jump and dance on the raft.

62
00:05:25.277 --> 00:05:28.564
Then I heard the sound of paddling behind the raft.

63
00:05:28.565 --> 00:05:31.193
The next lightning flash revealed the truth.

64
00:05:31.194 --> 00:05:36.597
It was the duke and the king in a rowboat, catching up with us.

